                                                "example_id": "c179fd2d-210f-4b88-a6fa-6f563f692d04",
                                                "sense_id": "21834f29-4fbc-30b9-961e-64f7003a3abc",
                                                "text": "Today, it is probably true to say that both varieties have positive prestige but for different reasons and to differing extents: attitudes to Swiss German, as the unifying vernacular that gives the German-Swiss their identity, are positive in every respect, while Swiss standard German enjoys widespread prestige only as a written form that enables them to be part of the international German-speaking community […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e07efc32-4cc0-49b4-b2ff-7d8655c2a7b1",
                                                "sense_id": "21834f29-4fbc-30b9-961e-64f7003a3abc",
                                                "text": "We do not intend this book to serve as a complete course in Swiss German; rather, it serves as a supplement to those studying the language in a more formal way."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2450c14b-02cb-3707-becf-5f50a807a618",
                                        "entry_id": "d10257e8-6bff-3e63-9ff2-7a1fe0bec002",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any local form of the German language used in Switzerland; Swiss Standard German."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
